#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186262960 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119841 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "489887a0-7013-5fb2-8f16-d18616196b0f" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Shortest Distance Between a Point and a Plane Given in Cartesian Form"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "98b0f40d-33e9-55be-8f3b-7f8eedd896c4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186261199} {:answer/id #uuid "bfb12be0-0f55-5f3e-88c4-ed8956e836d9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{23}{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186261569} {:answer/id #uuid "d3b6f646-82da-5b62-aee6-709895af763d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186261739} {:answer/id #uuid "f57cbc53-9eea-50bd-9941-2fb64d7aac6a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186262021} {:answer/id #uuid "f5d686d0-5802-573c-8388-4963787721a3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{17}{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186262026}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "98b0f40d-33e9-55be-8f3b-7f8eedd896c4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186261199} :answer-field/id #uuid "9fa62847-d308-543b-baa2-afe755afbc10" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186262411}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "875980ed-8584-5326-b58b-3349b4a511e1" :question/math-academy-id "q-129163" :question/problem "Find the shortest distance between the point $P(-2,5,-3)$ and the plane $Π$ with equation $4x-4y+2z=2.$" :question/worked-solution "Let's start by picking a point on the plane. To do that, we simply substitute some concrete values for $x$ and $y$ into the equation and solve for $z.$ Let's choose $x=1$ and $y=1$ (though it doesn't really matter what values we choose). Solving for $z,$ we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4x-4y+2z & =2 \\\\ 4(1)-4(1)+2z & =2 \\\\ 2z & =2 \\\\ z & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we get the point $Q(1,1,1)$ which lies on the plane.\n\nComputing $\\overset{\\to }{PQ},$ we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{PQ} & =⟨1,1,1⟩-⟨-2,5,-3⟩ \\\\  & =⟨3,-4,4⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe also need a normal vector to the plane. For any Cartesian equation of a plane $ax+by+cz=d,$ the normal vector is $n=⟨a,b,c⟩.$ So, for the plane $Π,$ we have $n=⟨4,-4,2⟩.$ \n\nFinally, the shortest distance from the point $P$ to the plane $Π$ is the absolute value of the scalar projection of $\\overset{\\to }{PQ}$ onto the normal vector of the plane:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}d & =|{\\text{comp}}_{n}\\,\\overset{\\to }{PQ}| \\\\  & =\\frac{|\\overset{\\to }{PQ}\\cdot n|}{|n|} \\\\  & =\\frac{|3\\cdot 4+(-4)\\cdot (-4)+4\\cdot 2|}{\\sqrt{{4}^{2}+(-4)^{2}+{2}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{|12+16+8|}{\\sqrt{16+16+4}} \\\\  & =\\frac{|36|}{\\sqrt{36}} \\\\  & =\\frac{36}{6} \\\\  & =6.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186120250 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119841 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "489887a0-7013-5fb2-8f16-d18616196b0f" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Shortest Distance Between a Point and a Plane Given in Cartesian Form"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a5c914f4-5a8b-548c-a5c2-f94ad127ef12" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186117660} {:answer/id #uuid "e142cff3-c8cc-592a-ad56-bb1b8e198189" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{62}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186117661} {:answer/id #uuid "00eddfed-b6f0-56e7-ae4c-5028b970d7c6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186117662} {:answer/id #uuid "2d32c0ff-487f-539b-9acc-2fcc848f4231" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186117663} {:answer/id #uuid "6601c7bc-b43b-5770-bdcb-2d6468033d70" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{17}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186117664}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "00eddfed-b6f0-56e7-ae4c-5028b970d7c6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186117662} :answer-field/id #uuid "20e14158-31b8-583a-aedb-9f5f098f4e19" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186117659}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "6cd2b067-45df-537d-b860-ed07175f92e4" :question/math-academy-id "q-33464" :question/problem "Find the shortest distance between the point $P(5,9,-6)$ and the plane $Π$ with equation $3x+2y+7z=-9.$" :question/worked-solution "Let's start by picking a point on the plane. To do that, we simply substitute some concrete values for $x$ and $y$ into the equation and solve for $z.$ Let's choose $x=2$ and $y=3$ (though it doesn't really matter what values we choose). Solving for $z,$ we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3x+2y+7z & =-9 \\\\ 3(2)+2(3)+7z & =-9 \\\\ 7z & =-21 \\\\ z & =-3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we get the point $Q(2,3,-3)$ which lies on the plane.\n\nComputing $\\overset{\\to }{PQ},$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{PQ} & =⟨2,3,-3⟩-⟨5,9,-6⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-3,-6,3⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe also need a normal vector to the plane. For any Cartesian equation of a plane $ax+by+cz=d,$ the normal vector is $n=⟨a,b,c⟩.$ So, for the plane $Π,$ we have $n=⟨3,2,7⟩.$ \n\nFinally, the shortest distance from the point $P$ to the plane $Π$ is the absolute value of the scalar projection of $\\overset{\\to }{PQ}$ onto the normal vector of the plane:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}d & =|{\\text{comp}}_{n}\\,\\overset{\\to }{PQ}| \\\\  & =\\frac{|\\overset{\\to }{PQ}\\cdot n|}{|n|} \\\\  & =\\frac{|(-3)\\cdot 3+(-6)\\cdot 2+3\\cdot 7|}{\\sqrt{{3}^{2}+{2}^{2}+{7}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{|-9-12+21|}{\\sqrt{9+4+49}} \\\\  & =\\frac{|\\,0\\,|}{\\sqrt{62}} \\\\  & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the point $P$ lies on the plane."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186120295 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119840 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "5a50c5f1-fbda-5c87-afa2-32495c69c18d" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Shortest Distance Between a Point and a Plane Given in Simplified Dot Product Form"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5cdb367a-ee31-52bd-8e49-76ea1a5deb03" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{10\\sqrt{42}}{21}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312716} {:answer/id #uuid "81295061-9129-54aa-abdf-5c3501c97825" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{7}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313016} {:answer/id #uuid "b83ec77e-cb86-58e7-b5e7-11f319ededff" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313407} {:answer/id #uuid "c84ad60d-9ec0-5f78-8c5d-b836c1212756" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{11\\sqrt{42}}{21}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313539} {:answer/id #uuid "e03a1af2-0bc1-5341-b0a6-801b7d85e33d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{4\\sqrt{42}}{21}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313740}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b83ec77e-cb86-58e7-b5e7-11f319ededff" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313407} :answer-field/id #uuid "aeb3b460-9b49-5397-9192-f15cd9be5b1d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186314481}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "6b172ee6-d9cd-537d-b8f8-03c5ed9b48c1" :question/math-academy-id "q-34062" :question/problem "Given that $Q(4,0,-3)$ lies on the plane $Π:r\\cdot ⟨1,-4,5⟩=-11$, find the shortest distance from $P(-2,1,-1)$ to $Π.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we find\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{PQ} & =⟨4,0,-3⟩-⟨-2,1,-1⟩ \\\\  & =⟨6,-1,-2⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the equation of a plane, we get a normal vector $n=⟨1,-4,5⟩.$\n\nFinally, the shortest distance from the point $P$ to the plane $Π$ is the absolute value of the scalar projection of $\\overset{\\to }{PQ}$ onto the normal vector of the plane:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}d & =|{\\text{comp}}_{n}\\,\\overset{\\to }{PQ}| \\\\  & =\\frac{|\\overset{\\to }{PQ}\\cdot n|}{|n|} \\\\  & =\\frac{|6\\cdot 1+(-1)\\cdot (-4)+(-2)\\cdot 5|}{\\sqrt{{1}^{2}+(-4)^{2}+{5}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{|6+4-10|}{\\sqrt{1+16+25}} \\\\  & =\\frac{|\\,0\\,|}{\\sqrt{42}} \\\\  & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the point $P$ lies on the plane $Π.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186348324 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119840 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "5a50c5f1-fbda-5c87-afa2-32495c69c18d" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Shortest Distance Between a Point and a Plane Given in Simplified Dot Product Form"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0ea53033-050f-51bc-b1f7-d809e2c747fe" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{13}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186345473} {:answer/id #uuid "15e2daf7-c934-50bc-ae67-edd8a7622e14" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "13\\sqrt{20}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186345541} {:answer/id #uuid "4b334642-8d19-5d6c-b2b1-468b896c54c0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{13\\sqrt{5}}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186345997} {:answer/id #uuid "a56010e2-ec46-5521-a5cd-8ec3d456b5a4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\sqrt{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186346794} {:answer/id #uuid "c4ca087f-3cf0-544b-a843-4b5a0d5368c2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186347053}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4b334642-8d19-5d6c-b2b1-468b896c54c0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{13\\sqrt{5}}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186345997} :answer-field/id #uuid "9ea9fa5e-7580-5121-9429-ea3965fd0aec" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186347881}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "799391e6-f2b4-56d4-b2e4-fcfb4ba4b2c4" :question/math-academy-id "q-80049" :question/problem "Given that $Q(1,3,4)$ lies on the plane $Π:r\\cdot ⟨-4,2,0⟩=2$, find the shortest distance from $P(5,-2,3)$ to $Π.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we find\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{PQ} & =⟨1,3,4⟩-⟨5,-2,3⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-4,5,1⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the equation of the plane, we get the normal vector $n=⟨-4,2,0⟩.$\n\nFinally, the shortest distance from the point $P$ to the plane $Π$ is the absolute value of the scalar projection of $\\overset{\\to }{PQ}$ onto the normal vector of the plane:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}d & =|{\\text{comp}}_{n}\\,\\overset{\\to }{PQ}| \\\\  & =\\frac{|\\overset{\\to }{PQ}\\cdot n|}{|n|} \\\\  & =\\frac{|(-4)\\cdot (-4)+5\\cdot 2+1\\cdot 0|}{\\sqrt{(-4)^{2}+{2}^{2}+{0}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{|16+10+0|}{\\sqrt{16+4+0}} \\\\  & =\\frac{|26|}{\\sqrt{20}} \\\\  & =\\frac{13\\sqrt{5}}{5}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186348334 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119841 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "489887a0-7013-5fb2-8f16-d18616196b0f" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Shortest Distance Between a Point and a Plane Given in Cartesian Form"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1ae5898c-91fd-500e-a18d-9a613793916b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186345586} {:answer/id #uuid "3bf469ee-bfa5-54ad-9ee7-3e8686851ee9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186345859} {:answer/id #uuid "547fec09-9ac4-53fe-bc5f-235373563b18" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186346067} {:answer/id #uuid "55089e0f-7f2d-5f0a-af43-9bef0b0757bb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{4}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186346071} {:answer/id #uuid "75641616-9478-59af-a091-d9b5df69b71f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186346385}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "55089e0f-7f2d-5f0a-af43-9bef0b0757bb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{4}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186346071} :answer-field/id #uuid "05a0dcf4-c48c-52c6-ad65-ce1c700d5ba5" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186347620}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "13132844-a558-54b3-bea9-4e5aeb81c059" :question/math-academy-id "q-80118" :question/problem "Find the shortest distance between the point $P(-7,5,2)$ and the plane $Π$ with equation $4x-8y+8z=-36.$" :question/worked-solution "Let's start by picking a point on the plane. To do that, we simply substitute some concrete values for $x$ and $y$ into the equation and solve for $z.$ Let's choose $x=-1$ and $y=1$ (though it doesn't really matter what values we choose). Solving for $z,$ we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4x-8y+8z & =-36 \\\\ 4(-1)-8(1)+8z & =-36 \\\\ 8z & =-24 \\\\ z & =-3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we get the point $Q(-1,1,-3)$ which lies on the plane.\n\nComputing $\\overset{\\to }{PQ},$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{PQ} & =⟨-1,1,-3⟩-⟨-7,5,2⟩ \\\\  & =⟨6,-4,-5⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe also need a normal vector to the plane. For any Cartesian equation of a plane $ax+by+cz=d,$ the normal vector is $n=⟨a,b,c⟩.$ So, for the plane $Π,$ we have $n=⟨4,-8,8⟩.$ \n\nFinally, the shortest distance from the point $P$ to the plane $Π$ is the absolute value of the scalar projection of $\\overset{\\to }{PQ}$ onto the normal vector of the plane:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}d & =|{\\text{comp}}_{n}\\,\\overset{\\to }{PQ}| \\\\  & =\\frac{|\\overset{\\to }{PQ}\\cdot n|}{|n|} \\\\  & =\\frac{|6\\cdot 4+(-4)\\cdot (-8)+(-5)\\cdot 8|}{\\sqrt{{4}^{2}+(-8)^{2}+{8}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{|24+32-40|}{\\sqrt{16+64+64}} \\\\  & =\\frac{|\\,16\\,|}{\\sqrt{144}} \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}]}
